pshot_surfaces.py) asserts CLI/lib/MCP/reconciler snapshot equivalence, but the 'MCP surface' and 'reconciler surface' blocks call compose_operation_snapshot(...) directly again with identical args rather than driving the actual MCP tool and reconciler __main__ entry points. Strengthen so those two slots exercise the real surfaces (surface-parity: a surface that performs the op but does not route through the shared composer is exactly where a parity bug hides). Acceptance: the MCP and reconciler blocks invoke their real entry points; mutation-perturbing the composer makes the surface assertions RED.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"bbb7-812e-4fe4-465d","ticket_type":"task","title":"Drive AC1 snapshot-equivalence contract through real MCP + reconciler entry points","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["58885abb-dd15-47d0-80c8-003b1a79d479","68c9c67d-f80a-4f09-9ebe-40e0822ec63f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787018845632864001,"uuid":"b8da3023-c211-4439-ada7-0a42f30b11c4"}